The process of setting up your own server for Minecraft will take only a few minutes nowadays, but finding a proper platform may be quite difficult, especially in Australia.
The query “best Minecraft server hosting” returns dozens of services offering the same lag-free guarantees, even though they take very different approaches. For Australian players, the choice comes down to a balance of hardware, price, mod support, and server location. In this article, we analyze the five best Minecraft server hosting providers for players in Australia.
#1. Godlike.Host— Best Overall / Best Value
The Godlike.Host server operates using its proprietary bare-metal hardware that includes the AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D and NVMe, whereas the regular server starts in less than two minutes. One of the unique advantages of this hosting service is the capability of managing the server through the Discord bot.
Pros:
- Forge, Fabric, Paper, and ready-to-use modpacks like RLCraft and ATM10;
- Pterodactyl-based panel and full SFTP access;
- Up to three free daily backups;
- Downtime-free RAM scaling;
- Free plan and 24/7 live support.
Cons:
- The free plan requires renewal every three hours;
- No hourly billing;
- Premium plans cost more than budget hosts.
Who it is for: beginners, casual players, modders, and growing communities.
